ChordChart
==========

Detects the chords of a song and prints a bar-aligned chord chart with key, tempo and
time signature. Works on local audio/video files and on video links (YouTube and other
sites supported by yt-dlp). Local use only. The chord and beat models come from madmom
(model files licensed CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, so non-commercial use only).

Setup (Windows)
---------------
    winget install --id Gyan.FFmpeg -e     # then open a new terminal
    uv sync                                # builds madmom from source (needs MSVC Build Tools)

Usage
-----
    uv run chordchart path/to/song.mp3
    uv run chordchart "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=..."
    uv run chordchart song.mp3 --start 1:05 --end 2:10    # just part of the song
    uv run chordchart song.mp3 --format json -o song.json
    uv run chordchart --help

Times in --start/--end are SS, MM:SS or H:MM:SS. Chart and JSON times always refer to
the original song, even when only a section is analysed.

Web page
--------
    uv run chordchart serve                 # opens http://127.0.0.1:8765/ in your browser
    uv run chordchart serve --port 9000 --no-browser
Paste a link (or a file path), optionally a start/end, press Analyze. Progress and the
chart appear on the page. The server only listens on this computer; Ctrl+C stops it.

Pasting YouTube links
---------------------
PowerShell splits an unquoted link at "&". Either quote it, or let chordchart ask:
    uv run chordchart                  # prompts: link, start, end (Enter = whole song)
    uv run chordchart --clipboard      # takes the link you just copied
Full links can be pasted as-is: playlist/radio parameters (&list=, &start_radio=,
&index=, ...) are ignored and only the video is analysed.

Download cache
--------------
Links are downloaded once and reused. Running the same link again needs no network.
    Location:  %LOCALAPPDATA%\chordchart\cache\downloads
               (set CHORDCHART_CACHE_DIR to use another folder; --help shows the path)
    uv run chordchart cache info       # location, number of downloads, size
    uv run chordchart cache clear      # delete all downloads
    uv run chordchart <link> --refresh # download that link again

If YouTube downloads start failing, upgrade yt-dlp:
    uv lock --upgrade-package yt-dlp && uv sync

Tests
-----
    uv run pytest                          # fast tests (no models, no network)
    uv run pytest -m "slow or not slow"    # plus the model tests
    uv run pytest -m network               # real YouTube downloads

